# Selected TT Domain and Boundary Condition Theorem v1

## Result

The analytic domain constraints are sourced, but the selected domain is not.

The constructive QG sources allow:

```text
bounded-geometry finite slab / bounded domain
Dirichlet or mixed boundary conditions
support restrictions away from the boundary
BRST-compatible boundary behavior with no boundary terms
```

This is enough to define model TT eigenpackets. It is not enough to select one
as the MTT TT spectrum.

## Candidate Domains

```text
flat periodic T3, L=2*pi       lambda_1 = 1
Dirichlet cube, L=1            lambda_1 = 3*pi^2
IR box, R -> infinity          lambda_1 -> 0
```

All three are execution models or regulators. None is promoted to the selected
MTT TT gap by the current corpus.

## Remaining Gate

The next gate is:

```text
TT_Domain_Selection_From_MTT_Fixed_Point_or_Internal_Quotient
```

It must supply a source rule selecting the TT domain, boundary condition,
dimensionless length/radius normalization, and zero-mode/Q-sector policy.
